(doc
  (title "YX Key Management Specification")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (para "**Status:** SPEC — v1 (2026-07-19) **Implements:** ADR D08 (see ybs-decisions.sxp) **Traceability:** security-architecture.sxp (HMAC key = mesh membership boundary)")
  (section
    (heading "1. Problem")
    (para "The YX HMAC key IS mesh membership: any holder can join, read, and inject. The historical \"development key\" is committed to (public) repos and hardcoded as a CLI default. Keys MUST live outside git, in an OS-encrypted store, and tools MUST resolve them at runtime."))
  (section
    (heading "2. Requirements")
    (item "R1: Keys are stored in the **macOS Keychain** (encrypted at rest, unlocked with the user session). No plaintext key files in any repo or dotfile.")
    (item "R2: A CLI (`yxkey`) manages keys: `set`, `get`, `list`, `remove`.")
    (item "R3: Key material never appears in argv or shell history — `set` reads from **stdin**; `get` prints to stdout only (for piping/subprocess use).")
    (item "R4: A key is 32 bytes, entered/displayed as 64 hex chars. `set` validates; `generate` creates a cryptographically random one.")
    (item "R5: Multiple meshes: keys are named. Keychain mapping: `service = \"org.spy.yx\"`, `account = <mesh-name>` (default mesh name: `mesh`).")
    (item "R6: All YX executables resolve keys in this order (first hit wins):")
    (item "1. explicit `--key <hex>` flag        (tests, overrides)")
    (item "2. `YX_KEY` environment variable      (CI, launchd plists w/ EnvironmentVariables)")
    (item "3. Keychain `org.spy.yx` / `--mesh <name>` account   (normal operation)")
    (item "4. built-in development key + a LOUD warning         (dev convenience only)")
    (item "R7: Python implementation reaches the Keychain via `security find-generic-password -s org.spy.yx -a <mesh> -w` (subprocess) — same resolution order, no new dependencies."))
  (section
    (heading "3. Non-goals (v1)")
    (item "Key rotation protocol over the mesh (manual: `yxkey set` on each node).")
    (item "Per-peer derived keys (KeyStore/KeyRotation already sketch this — unchanged).")
    (item "Non-macOS stores (future: file-based encrypted store or platform keyring)."))
  (section
    (heading "4. API contract")
    (code "yxkey generate [--mesh NAME]      create + store a random 32-byte key; prints hex
yxkey set      [--mesh NAME]      read 64-hex from stdin, validate, store (upsert)
yxkey get      [--mesh NAME]      print 64-hex to stdout (exit 1 if absent)
yxkey list                        list mesh names present in the Keychain
yxkey remove   [--mesh NAME]      delete the named key")
    (para "Swift: `MeshKey.load(mesh:explicit:)` in Primitives implements R6 and is used by yxCLI + yxnode. Python: `yx_key.resolve_key(args)` mirrors it for the python CLI."))
  (section
    (heading "5. Verification")
    (item "V1: `yxkey generate` → `yxkey get` round-trips 64 hex chars.")
    (item "V2: `set` rejects non-hex and wrong lengths.")
    (item "V3: yxCLI with no `--key` and Keychain populated uses the Keychain key (log shows `key source: keychain`), and interops with the python CLI resolving the same key via `security`.")
    (item "V4: with nothing configured, tools still run on the dev key but print the warning (grep-able: `WARNING: using built-in development key`)."))
  (section
    (heading "6. Future (recorded, not built)")
    (item "Bonjour/mDNS discovery (ADR D10) does not change key handling: discovery ≠ membership; the HMAC key remains the trust boundary.")
    (item "`yxkey rotate` — regenerate + optional mesh-wide announce once node daemons can coordinate.")))
